# Single-owner release handoff

Codex currently owns the integrated Website + Workspace release. When a Cursor
task is finished:

1. Commit scoped files (no secrets, no logo preview PNGs, no leftover `.cursor/COLLABORATION.md` unless the note is for this ship).
2. Push only the named feature branch, never `main`.
3. Create a preview if useful and run focused tests/build checks.
4. Hand the commit SHA, changed files, migrations, environment requirements, and
   verification evidence to Codex.
5. Do not run a production deployment, promote, pin aliases, or change Vercel
   project settings while Codex owns the release.

“Done” means ready for handoff; it is not independent production authorization.

## Target

Sheetomatic only (`sheetomatic.com` / `app.sheetomatic.com`). Named portals (Hingorani / Tops / Anmol) still need an explicit deploy request.

## Forward-only (from 2026-10-22)

See `.cursor/rules/production-forward-only.mdc`. Only newer commits than the locked baseline may serve production.

## Do not skip

If Auto-review blocks push/deploy, retry once with `request_smart_mode_approval` and the exact block reason.
